  "type": "singleCorrect",
  "level": 2,
  "question": {
    "text": "The equation of the right bisector plane of the segment joining (2,3,4) and (6,7,8) is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wh77M",
      "text": "$x+y+z+15=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "frEu9",
      "text": "$x+y+z-15=0$",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "wAnEk",
      "text": "$x-y+z-15=0$",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "4xr7b",
      "text": "None of these",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "If the given points be $A(2,3,4)$ and $B$ $(6,7,8),$ then their mid-point $\\mathrm{N}(4,5,6)$ must lie on the plane. The direction ratios of $\\mathrm{AB}$ are $4,4,4,$ i.e. 1,1,1\r\n\r\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/FWpePhV8gc4X4C6HfEhqdq70nJpMuPNrtv7yGm7p36k.original.fullsize.png\"><br>\r\n\r\n$\\therefore$ The required plane passes through $\\mathrm{N}(4,5,6)$ and is normal to $\\mathrm{AB}$. Thus its equation is\r\n\r\n$$\r\n\r\n1(x-4)+1(y-5)+1(z-6)=0 \\Rightarrow x+y+z=15\r\n\r\n$$",
    "image": null
  },
